icates that the 'left' pointer is incremented (left +=3D 1). The bottom sec=
tion illustrates the updated state after the pointer increment, where the '=
left' pointer now points to -2.  The 'right' pointer remains unchanged. The=
 dotted arrow emphasizes the movement of the 'left' pointer.  The overall d=
iagram demonstrates a single iteration of the algorithm, highlighting the p=
